scope: |
  SSC3-13d — the owner's spelling for the prelude's Dataset: `def of[T](items: T*): Dataset[T]`,
  asked for 2026-08-14 right after SSC3-13c made `of` a vararg. (`v3/SPRINT.md` is claimed by
  `bench-b4-three-version-table`, so the plan is here — in git, before the edit.)

  THE SIGNATURE ONLY READS AS TRUE IF THE CLASS TAKES THE PARAMETER TOO, so the change is
  `case class Dataset[T](items: List[T])` with the members written in terms of `T` —
  `first(): Option[T]`, `filter(p: T => Boolean): Dataset[T]`, `map[U](f: T => U): Dataset[U]`.
  Giving `of` a `Dataset[T]` return over a non-generic class would be a signature describing
  something that is not there.

  AT TIER 0 THIS IS DOCUMENTATION, NOT ENFORCEMENT — invariant I-2 — so it MUST be behaviour-free,
  and that is a claim to measure rather than assume. `Param.tpe` text is not inert: `Lower` reads it
  for instance resolution (`resolveGivenArgs` unifies type TEXT), so swapping `Any` for `T` across
  thirty signatures in the file every program loads is worth N.

  PROBED BEFORE THE PRELUDE DEPENDED ON IT: a generic case class with a generic vararg companion
  (`case class Box[T]` + `def of[T](xs: T*): Box[T]`) runs on both fronts.

  MEASUREMENT: N with floors DIFF 3 and CRASH 9, plus the dataset corpus cases read INDIVIDUALLY —
  a bucket count can hide one case moving PASS -> DIFF while another moves back.
next: measure, gate, push
